    <string name="skills_help">How do skill levels work?</string>
    <string name="skills_how_points" formatted="false">• Every set you tick counts for its skill: program days, repeated days and your own workouts. A class counts once you\'ve done 20% of it.\n\n• A skill is a move you do on your own, from a dead hang to a one-arm handstand: 40 in all. Assisted, banded, supported and lowering-only versions are steps toward them and earn no level, and neither do helpers like chin-ups or knee raises.\n\n• Each skill has five levels: Beginner, Intermediate, Advanced, Master and Elite, at 10, 15, 20, 25 and 30 sets at its target. A target is a working set with a rep or two left in you, not your max. On one-sided moves, your weaker side counts. A skill\'s page lists its targets.\n\n• Harder counts for easier: a bigger set counts for the lower targets, and a set on a harder rung counts for the easier rungs of its ladder.\n\n• A hold counts from when the shape is set until it breaks. A rep starts still, goes through full range and never kicks or swings.\n\n• Did more or fewer than planned? Tap \"Did more or fewer?\" under the set. Count only clean reps.\n\n• Harder days add a quarter to strength reps and holds, so you reach targets sooner.\n\n• By the end of Level 10 every skill reaches Master. The top rung of each ladder gets about 24 of its 30 Elite sets in the classes; the rest is yours: repeat days, go Harder or add your own workouts.\n\n• The outline shows how hard a skill is, green to red. The shield shows your level, from one band (Beginner) to the winged star (Elite).\n\n• Switched a skill off in Settings? Your score counts the skills you train; the leaderboard keeps the full scale.\n\n• Skipped days give nothing: placement, Complete day and Complete level don\'t count.\n\n• Your overall score, out of 100, adds up each ladder\'s best skill: harder skills and higher levels add more.</string>
